# Build-time shim: resolve webkit2gtk-4.0 to 4.1.
#
# webview_go hardcodes `#cgo linux pkg-config: gtk+-3.0 webkit2gtk-4.0` and has
# cut no release since Aug 2024 (its master still says 4.0), so the module
# cannot ask for 4.1 itself. WebKitGTK 4.1 is the *same C API* as 4.0, rebuilt
# against libsoup3 instead of the unmaintained libsoup2 — only the pkg-config
# name and include directory differ — so satisfying the 4.0 request from 4.1 is
# sound rather than a version fudge.
#
# It has to be 4.1: webkit2gtk-4.0 was dropped from the Ubuntu archive in 24.04
# (which is what `ubuntu-latest` resolves to), while 4.1 is present from 22.04
# onwards on amd64. Linking 4.0 would break the release build and produce a
# .deb/.rpm whose library cannot be resolved on any current distro.
#
# Consumed via PKG_CONFIG_PATH from `make build-desktop` and the package
# builds (debian/rules, the RPM spec); it is a build input only and is never
# installed.
#
# TODO: delete this file, and the PKG_CONFIG_PATH it needs, once webview_go
# releases a version whose cgo directive names webkit2gtk-4.1.

Name: WebKitGTK 4.0 to 4.1 shim
Description: Satisfies webview_go's webkit2gtk-4.0 request from webkit2gtk-4.1
Version: 4.1
Requires: webkit2gtk-4.1
